# clang-tidy configuration for virmux — enforced as a zero-findings CI gate.
#
# Enabled families:
#   bugprone-*        likely bugs (unchecked conversions, swallowed errors, ...)
#   clang-analyzer-*  path-sensitive static analysis (null derefs, dead stores,
#                     leaks, blocking calls inside critical sections, ...)
#   performance-*     avoidable copies / allocations with mechanical fixes
#
# Exclusions (each is a deliberate decision, not a suppression of real bugs):
#   bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
#       Fires on nearly every function taking two ints/strings (e.g. POSIX-style
#       (fd, flags) or (path, mode) signatures). Fixing it would mean wrapping
#       every scalar in a strong type, which is out of proportion for this
#       codebase; the signal-to-noise ratio is too low to gate CI on.
#   bugprone-signed-bitwise
#       Flags the standard POSIX flag idiom (O_WRONLY | O_CREAT, S_IRUSR | ...)
#       because the libc macros are signed ints. These expressions are correct
#       by definition of the POSIX API and cannot be rewritten without casts
#       that would only obscure them.
#   performance-enum-size
#       Suggests shrinking every enum's underlying type to uint8_t. None of our
#       enums are stored in bulk, so there is no measurable gain, and the
#       underlying type is a deliberate interface decision: IpcMsgType is the
#       16-bit message-type field of the IPC wire protocol and must stay
#       uint16_t. The rest of performance-* is enforced.
#
# Every finding is an error (WarningsAsErrors). Only the project's own headers
# are analysed; the vendored Unity test framework (tests/unity) and system
# headers are excluded. Use NOLINT only for genuine false positives, always as
# `NOLINT(check-name): reason`.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise,
  -performance-enum-size
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(include/virmux|src)/.*\.(h|hpp)$'
ExcludeHeaderFilterRegex: '.*/tests/unity/.*'
